---
import { css } from 'styled-system/css'
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Callout from 'web-design-system/astro/marketing/Callout.astro'
import CodeBlock from 'web-design-system/astro/product/CodeBlock.astro'
import TableScroll from '../../../components/TableScroll.astro'

const toc = [
  { label: 'Workspace layout', href: '#workspace-layout' },
  { label: 'The desktop app', href: '#desktop-app' },
  { label: 'The agent side', href: '#agent-side' },
  { label: 'Persistence', href: '#persistence' },
  { label: 'Web surfaces', href: '#web-surfaces' },
  { label: 'Specs', href: '#specs' },
]

const tree = `todo-lofi/
├── apps/
│   ├── todo-2/                # GPUI desktop application
│   └── agent-cli/             # terminal agent + ACP server
├── libs/
│   ├── storage/               # SQLite persistence, migrations, sync tables
│   ├── acp-client/            # Agent Client Protocol client
│   ├── ai_providers/          # LLM provider abstraction
│   ├── gpui-tokio/            # GPUI <-> Tokio bridge
│   ├── report_proc/           # proc-macro crate
│   ├── web-design-system/     # Panda/Solid design system (not a crate)
│   └── ...                    # CRDT experiments (dson, op_crdt)
├── demos/
│   └── design-system-showcase # component gallery + page replicas
├── apps/docs-web/             # this documentation site
├── patched/                   # vendored upstream forks
├── docs/                      # specs, agent skills, images
└── flake.nix                  # devShell: Rust, cargo-watch, Node, pnpm`

const apps = [
  {
    name: 'apps/todo-2',
    role: 'The desktop application',
    detail:
      'GPUI views and app state: task lists and details, the agent pane, mini-apps, sync panes, and settings.',
  },
  {
    name: 'apps/agent-cli',
    role: 'The terminal agent',
    detail:
      'A full-screen TUI, a provider/model registry with fallback combos, sub-agents, and an ACP server over stdio.',
  },
  {
    name: 'libs/storage',
    role: 'Persistence',
    detail:
      'The SQLite data model and migrations: tasks, tags and tag settings, repeats, trips, workflows, Todoist, GitHub, and managed apps.',
  },
  {
    name: 'libs/acp-client',
    role: 'Agent plumbing',
    detail:
      'Launches agent processes, owns sessions and the transcript model, and provides the file-system and terminal capabilities an agent session needs.',
  },
  {
    name: 'libs/ai_providers',
    role: 'Model access',
    detail:
      'OpenAI-compatible provider implementations on top of the cersei agent library, including an OAuth-backed provider.',
  },
  {
    name: 'libs/gpui-tokio',
    role: 'Runtime bridge',
    detail: 'Runs Tokio futures from GPUI entities so async work never blocks the UI thread.',
  },
]

const desktopModules = [
  { name: 'main.rs', detail: 'Application entry point and window setup.' },
  { name: 'store.rs', detail: 'The app-level store that entities read and write.' },
  { name: 'projects.rs', detail: 'Project and area tree state.' },
  { name: 'theme.rs', detail: 'The desktop palette. Deliberately independent of the web design system.' },
  { name: 'ui_parts/', detail: 'The panes: task list and row, task details, agent pane, mini-apps, integrations, automations, pickers, settings, notifications, navbar.' },
  { name: 'coding_git.rs, coding_mcp.rs', detail: 'Git and MCP support for coding workflow runs.' },
  { name: 'components/', detail: 'Reusable widgets: calendar, checkbox, date/time picker, mini task list, tag chip.' },
]

const specs = [
  { file: 'workflow-engine-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'Workflow engine data model in libs/storage, minimal UI contract.' },
  { file: 'workflow-simplification-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'The v2 workflow model; supersedes the v1 data model.' },
  { file: 'coding-workflow-runs-spec.md', status: 'Implemented', topic: 'AI-assisted feature development runs: phases, state, and review.' },
  { file: 'coding-workflow-subtasks-spec.md', status: 'Proposed', topic: 'Subtasks inside a run and coverage of the spec they implement.' },
  { file: 'todoist-sync-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'Todoist import plus immediate push of title/description/done deltas.' },
  { file: 'github-integration-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'GitHub issues/projects sync and a git-backed coding workflow.' },
  { file: 'acp-client-and-agent-panel-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'The ACP client crate and the todo-2 agent panel that drives it.' },
  { file: 'todo2-agent-pane-ui-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'The agent pane UI: layout, states, and interactions.' },
  { file: 'agent-cli-interview-feature-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'The /interview command that turns a request into a spec.' },
  { file: 'todo2-managed-apps-spec.md', status: 'Draft v2', topic: 'Managed tags, sections, and tasks — the model behind mini-apps.' },
  { file: 'todo2-nested-projects-spec.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'Nesting project directories under tags.' },
  { file: 'symphony.md', status: 'Draft v1', topic: 'A language-agnostic service specification.' },
  { file: 'web-design-system-spec.md', status: 'Implemented v1', topic: 'The web design system and its showcase.' },
]
---

<Docs
  title="Architecture"
  description="A Cargo workspace for the app and its libraries, plus a pnpm workspace for the web surfaces. Here is how the pieces relate."
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="workspace-layout">Workspace layout</h2>
  <CodeBlock filename="todo-lofi" code={tree} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <p>
    <code>Cargo.toml</code> declares members as <code>apps/*</code>, <code>libs/*</code>, and
    <code>demos/*</code>, and explicitly excludes the three JavaScript packages so{' '}
    <code>cargo check --workspace</code> never walks their trees.
  </p>

  <h2 id="desktop-app">The desktop app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>apps/todo-2</code> is GPUI all the way down: one window, a handful of panes, and entities that
    hold state. Async work (sync, agent sessions, file reads) is pushed onto Tokio through{' '}
    <code>libs/gpui-tokio</code> and applied back on the UI thread.
  </p>
  <TableScroll label="Desktop app modules">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Module</th>
          <th>Responsibility</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          desktopModules.map((module) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{module.name}</code></td>
              <td>{module.detail}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>
  <Callout tone="note" title="Two themes, on purpose">
    <code>apps/todo-2/src/theme.rs</code> is the desktop palette. It is intentionally not generated from
    the web design system's tokens — the two surfaces share no code, and the design system spec lists that
    as a non-goal.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="agent-side">The agent side</h2>
  <p>
    There is one agent implementation and two front ends. <code>apps/agent-cli</code> is a terminal TUI
    that also speaks the Agent Client Protocol over stdio; <code>libs/acp-client</code> is the client that
    the desktop app's agent pane uses to talk to that same protocol. Provider selection, model fallback
    combos, MCP servers, hooks, and sub-agents all live on the CLI side and are shared.
  </p>
  <TableScroll label="Workspace crates">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Crate</th>
          <th>Role</th>
          <th>What it contains</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          apps.map((app) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{app.name}</code></td>
              <td>{app.role}</td>
              <td>{app.detail}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>

  <h2 id="persistence">Persistence</h2>
  <p>
    <code>libs/storage</code> owns the database. It is SQLite, accessed through the toasty ORM, and it
    carries its own migration binary:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>task.rs</code>, <code>tag.rs</code>, <code>tag_settings.rs</code> — the core task model.</li>
    <li><code>repeat.rs</code> — recurring rules.</li>
    <li><code>workflow.rs</code> — workflow definitions and run state.</li>
    <li><code>todoist.rs</code>, <code>github.rs</code>, <code>external.rs</code> — sync mappings for outside systems.</li>
    <li><code>managed.rs</code>, <code>link.rs</code>, <code>trip.rs</code> — the models behind mini-apps, links, and trips.</li>
    <li><code>migrations.rs</code> and <code>src/bin/</code> — schema migrations, driven by the <code>mig</code> command.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The remaining <code>libs/*</code> crates are narrower: <code>ai_providers</code> and
    <code>gpui-tokio</code> are infrastructure, <code>report_proc</code> and
    <code>derive_entity_id</code> are macros, and <code>dson_freeform_task</code>,
    <code>dson_typed_task</code>, and <code>op_crdt</code> are CRDT experiments for conflict-free task
    data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="web-surfaces">Web surfaces</h2>
  <p>
    Two web apps share one design system, and none of them touch the Rust workspace:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>libs/web-design-system</code> — tokens, a Panda preset, Ark UI headless primitives, and styled
      Solid components with <code>.astro</code> wrappers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>demos/design-system-showcase</code> — the component gallery and the page shapes the design
      system is built from.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>apps/docs-web</code> — this site. It consumes the design system's preset and the marketing
      docs components rather than restyling them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    See the design system's <code>DESIGN.md</code> for the token and layering rules, and
    <a href="/docs/contributor/contributing">Contributing</a> for the checks that keep them honest.
  </p>

  <h2 id="specs">Specs</h2>
  <p>
    Non-trivial features are specified before they are built. Each spec records the decisions taken during
    the interview that produced it, so the file is the rationale as well as the design.
  </p>
  <TableScroll label="Specs">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Spec</th>
          <th>Status</th>
          <th>Covers</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          specs.map((spec) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{spec.file}</code></td>
              <td>{spec.status}</td>
              <td>{spec.topic}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>
  <p class={css({ fontSize: 'sm', color: 'fg.subtle' })}>
    All specs live in <code>docs/spec/</code> at the repository root.
  </p>
</Docs>
